---
smd: 1
title: Quotes and backslashes in attribute values
summary: Pins how quoted attribute values read, so later releases are compared against them. Since 1.10 a quoted value may hold its own quote, escaped with a backslash; every other backslash stays as written.
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-15
---

## Escaped quotes

:::note{title="It's \"done\""}
A title with both kinds of quote, written as `smd fmt` writes it.
:::

Activation :metric[42%]{label="The \"active\" users' share" trend=up} this week.

:::decision{title='Keep "v1" reading' status=accepted}
A value with only double quotes is single-quoted, without escapes.
:::

## Backslashes that are not escapes

:::note{title="C:\Users\docs\plan.smd"}
A Windows path keeps its backslashes.
:::

:::note{title="\\server\share"}
Two backslashes stay two backslashes.
:::

:::note{title="C:\docs\"}
A value that ends with a backslash, valid before 1.10, reads as it did.
:::
